Certainly! Here's a JavaScript function that will switch the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function swapAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    if (words[i] === "beautiful" || words[i] === "green") {
      adjectives.push(words[i]);
    }
  }

  if (adjectives.length > 1) {
    const firstAdjective = adjectives.shift();
    adjectives.push(firstAdjective);
  }

  return words.join(" ");
}

const originalSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const modifiedSentence = swapAdjectives(originalSentence);
console.log(modifiedSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function splits the input sentence into individual words, filters out the adjectives ("beautiful" and "green" in this case), and then swaps their positions in the array. Finally, it joins the words back together into a new sentence.

