3. The right to cancel a contract within a certain period of time, usually 14 days, and receive a full refund.
4. The right to claim compensation for any losses incurred due to a breach of contract by the seller.
5. The right to have goods repaired or replaced if they are found to be defective within a reasonable time frame.

These rights are designed to protect consumers from unfair practices and ensure that they receive fair treatment when purchasing goods and services.

