To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, go to the "Applications" tab and click on your newly created application.
3. Click on the "Settings" tab and scroll down to the "Allowed Callback URLs" section. Add the callback URLs for each of your React apps.
4. In your React apps, install the `@auth0/auth0-react` library using npm or yarn.
5. Create a new file called `auth0-config.js` in your app's root directory and add the following code:
```javascript
import auth0 from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const auth0ClientId = 'your_client_id';
const auth0Domain = 'your_domain.com';

auth0.useAuth0({
  clientId: auth0ClientId,
  domain: auth0Domain,
  redirectUri: window.location.origin,
});

export default auth0;
```
Replace `your_client_id` with your actual Auth0 client ID and `your_domain.com` with your Auth0 domain.
6. In your app's main component, import the `auth0` object and use it to authenticate users. For example:
```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { auth0 } from './auth0-config';

function App() {
  const [isAuthenticated, setIsAuthenticated] = useState(false);

  async function handleAuthentication() {
    try {
      await auth0.loginWithRedirect();
      setIsAuthenticated(true);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error authenticating:', error);
    }
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {!isAuthenticated && (
        <button onClick={handleAuthentication}>Login</button>
      )}
      {isAuthenticated && (
        <p>You are logged in!</p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```
